//==
// # Edge discretization: types
//
// One polyline per model edge, made under chordal, angular, and length criteria and consumed by
// both faces adjacent to the edge, one of them through `Reversed`. See README.md in this folder
// for the mathematics and the decisions.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Criteria
//  - Discretizations
//  - Parameter-space images
//  - Refinement requests

//==
// Criteria

// An optional upper bound: `Unlimited` imposes nothing, `AtMost(Value)` bounds a length in model
// units.
type Limit
    = Unlimited
    | AtMost(Value: Number);

// What a discretization of an edge must satisfy. `Chordal` bounds the distance between each chord
// and the arc it replaces (model units). `Angular` bounds the turning angle between consecutive
// segments; each segment's chord stays within half of it of every tangent of its arc (see
// `TangentDeviation`). `MaxLength` bounds every chord. `MinLength` is the floor below which
// refinement stops: a segment is split for a criterion only when both halves are at least this
// long, which makes every refinement terminate. `MinSegments` is the least segment count of a
// closed edge; it is never taken below 3 (`ClosedEdgeMinimum`). Model-independent: the model's
// own tolerances are applied on top by the `Effective*` functions.
type DiscretizationCriteria
    implements IValue
{
    Chordal: Number;
    Angular: Angle;
    MaxLength: Limit;
    MinLength: Number;
    MinSegments: Integer;
}

// A per-edge minimum segment count, indexed by `BrepEdgeIndex`. Empty by default (`NoFloors`); an
// index past the end means no floor. The hook through which quad count matching asks for equal
// counts on opposite sides of a structured face.
type SegmentFloors
{
    ByEdge: Array<Integer>;
}

//==
// Discretizations

// The polyline of one model edge. `Parameters` are in the edge curve's own parameter and strictly
// monotone; `Points[i]` is the curve evaluated at `Parameters[i]`, except that the two end points
// are the vertex points exactly (copied, never evaluated). A canonical discretization (every result
// of `Discretize` and every entry of `EdgeDiscretizations`) runs from the edge domain's start to
// its end, parameters strictly increasing; `Reversed` produces the other direction, which exists
// only while a face consumes it. A degenerate edge has two parameters and one repeated point.
// An edge that `CanDiscretize` rejects gets the empty value (`Undiscretized`): no parameters and
// no points, so the table keeps one entry per edge and no face citing that edge is meshed.
type EdgeDiscretization
{
    Edge: BrepEdgeIndex;
    Parameters: Array<Number>;
    Points: Array<Point3D>;
}

// The canonical discretization of every edge of a model, indexed by `BrepEdgeIndex`:
// `ByEdge[i].Edge.Value == i`. The single source both faces of an edge read from.
type EdgeDiscretizations
{
    ByEdge: Array<EdgeDiscretization>;
}

//==
// Parameter-space images

// One parameter space in which an edge's polyline is drawn: a face that uses the edge, and the
// pcurve of the edge on that face's surface. `Pcurve` is none (`Value` -1) when the edge's curve
// carries no pcurve on that surface; the image is then made by `Project`. A seam edge has two
// images on its one face, one per pcurve. The `UvCoordinate`s of an image hold natural surface
// parameters (an angle in radians, a length), not normalized ones.
type EdgeImage
    implements IValue
{
    Face: BrepFaceIndex;
    Pcurve: PcurveIndex;
}

//==
// Refinement requests

// Why face meshing asks for a finer polyline on an edge: the face's loops cross in parameter space,
// a segment is too long for the face's parameter-space test, or a structured quad grid needs a
// higher count on this side.
type RefinementReason
    = LoopSelfIntersects
    | TooCoarseInParameterSpace
    | QuadCountMismatch;

// A request from face meshing for a finer polyline on one edge. `Chordal` is the chordal bound to
// refine to (the current one when the request is about counts only); `Segments` is the least
// segment count wanted, 0 when the request is not about counts. Several requests on one edge
// combine: the smallest `Chordal`, the largest `Segments`.
type EdgeRefinementRequest
    implements IValue
{
    Edge: BrepEdgeIndex;
    Reason: RefinementReason;
    Chordal: Number;
    Segments: Integer;
}
